<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav December industry output falls 2 percent.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav December industry output falls 2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT  Dec 96	Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p> pct change mth/mth	    - 2.0	 - 7.2	 n.a.</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr		+ 4.8	 +14.4	 n.a.</p>
<p> index (base average 1995)   116.2	 118.6	 n.a.</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE DATA (Jan-Dec)</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr		+ 7.1	 + 7.4	 n.a.</p>
<p>SEASONALLY ADJUSTED DATA</p>
<p> index (base average 1995)   106.3	 113.2	 n.a.</p>
<p>NOTES -- Industrial output in December 1996 was 41.2 percent down against the same month in 1991.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-December 1996 industry output was 44.5 percent below the same figure for 1991.</p>
<p>Data largely exclude the private sector, where manufacturing is not significant. -- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 2224305</p>
